# Tier 2a: lazy early-exit propagation filter, a thread-local depth-0
# abstraction cache, removal of the matcher's remaining per-test heap
# allocations, and batched thread-local instrumentation counters.
#
# Applies on top of, in order:
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-macos-proc.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-instrumentation-v3.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-online-subsumption-v3.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-perf-v3.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-tier1-v3.patch
# against the pinned upstream commit 0b5d09c47446096f9e3a0812b35afc72b7f2a718.
# Apply with:  patch -V none -p1 -i <this file>
#
# The Isabelle/HOL-extracted checker (checker/) is not touched. Only two files
# change: src/output_set/subsume.rs and src/instrument.rs.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE MEASUREMENTS SAID, BEFORE ANY CODE WAS WRITTEN
#
# 8.84 million real matcher input pairs were dumped from n=9 and n=10 search,
# prune-all and gen-proof runs and profiled. The search tree inside the exact
# test is essentially trivial:
#
#   nodes per test, rejecting pairs:  1.058 (k=7)  1.059 (k=8)  1.487 (k=9)
#   ... of which single-node:          94.5 %       94.8 %       57.7 %
#   nodes per test, accepting pairs:  3.155        3.485        4.269
#   maximum node count over all 8.84 M pairs: 47
#
# So the cost of the exact test is NOT search. It is the 2*channels
# per-channel abstraction computations that the depth-0 filter performed
# EAGERLY, before comparing any of them. This patch attacks exactly that, and
# the Glasgow/Django search techniques the campaign was sent to transplant are
# rejected with measurement (see the bottom of this header).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#  A. Lazy outer side with early exit (SORTNETOPT_T2A_LAZY, default 1).
#     One side ("inner") is materialised in full; the other ("outer") is
#     computed one channel at a time and tested against every inner channel
#     immediately, so a domain wipeout can return after computing as few as
#     ONE abstraction instead of 2*channels.
#
#  B. Thread-local depth-0 abstraction cache (SORTNETOPT_T2A_D0CACHE,
#     default 1). 4 slots, keyed by channel count plus the set's live u64
#     words. At fixed_channels == 0 the working sets have not been permuted
#     yet, so a side's abstractions are a pure function of that side's
#     PackedSet. In the real workload one side is a FIXED query reused across
#     a long run of consecutive exact tests: measured 89.4 % (k=7) and 92.4 %
#     (k=8) of records repeat the previous record's `b` side, mean run length
#     9.4-13.2, max 2,299. Measured cache hit rate in-stack: 93.7 %.
#     This is a per-thread cache of a deterministically recomputable value. It
#     is NOT a stored per-entry abstraction -- the memory-negative mistake M2a
#     measured and rejected -- and index memory is untouched.
#
#  C. Minimum-domain-first outer ordering (SORTNETOPT_T2A_MINDOM, default 0).
#     Implemented, measured, and DEFAULTED OFF because it did not pay: on real
#     corpora it cost about 1 % (k=8: 890 ns on / 880 ns off; k=9: 1,992 /
#     1,979). The code and the gate are retained so the measurement stays
#     reproducible.
#
#  D. The matcher's remaining per-test heap allocations are removed. Tier 1
#     removed the two Vec<bool> output-set allocations but left three: the
#     abstraction scratch buffer, the undo stack, and the deep-node inner
#     buffer. A fresh `Subsume` is built per exact test, so each was one
#     malloc+free per test. They now come from a thread-local pool.
#
#  E. Batched thread-local instrumentation counters. THIS IS THE LARGEST
#     SINGLE IN-STACK EFFECT IN THE PATCH, and it is a fix to a cost Tier 1
#     introduced and flagged but did not quantify. `Subsume` is constructed
#     and dropped ~3.9 M times per n=10 search across 10 threads, and its
#     Drop flushed diagnostics with fetch_add on GLOBAL AtomicU64s. Measured
#     in-stack at n=10 on a quiet M4, 4 rounds each:
#         Tier-1 binary                                    3,373 ms
#         Tier-2a binary, ALL gates disabled (i.e. running
#           the ORIGINAL eager algorithm)                  3,812 ms
#     The new binary running the original algorithm was 13 % slower, which
#     isolates the cost to something paid regardless of the gates: the extra
#     contended atomics. Counters are now accumulated in a thread-local batch
#     and flushed every FLUSH_EVERY = 1024 tests, plus at thread exit, plus
#     via instrument::drain_all_batches() at report time (a registry of
#     Arc<Mutex<Batch>> is kept so rayon's unjoined prune/proof workers do not
#     lose counts). Counter names, output format and totals are unchanged.
#
# SOUNDNESS. Every edge removal the filter performs is justified either by
# abstraction-dominance failure -- a necessary condition for that channel
# pairing -- or by the pre-existing singleton-exclusivity rule. Both are sound
# regardless of the order in which pairs are examined, and `Subsume::search`
# is complete over whatever edges remain. Reordering the pair iteration and
# short-circuiting once a wipeout is detected therefore cannot change the
# accept/reject verdict; it can only change how much pruning happens, hence
# performance and which witness permutation is returned. Empirically the
# fixpoint is reached identically: subsume_nodes/subsume_calls is 1.2274 with
# the changes and 1.2288 without (0.11 % apart).
#
# Setting LAZY=0 D0CACHE=0 MINDOM=0 restores the original eager code path,
# which is kept intact and reachable, so all four transformations can be A/B'd
# inside one binary.
#
# New counters (per-`Subsume` usize fields folded into the thread-local batch,
# deliberately NOT per-call atomics, which would distort the very measurement
# they exist for): subsume_abstractions, subsume_d0_cache_hits,
# subsume_d0_cache_misses, subsume_filter_fail.
# subsume_abstractions is the campaign's headline work counter: it falls from
# 15.79 to 4.60 per exact test at n=10, a 3.43x reduction.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REJECTED WITH MEASUREMENT (details in evidence/v3/tier2a/report.md)
#
#  * Nogood recording + restarts, and independent-component decomposition
#    (survey techniques 3 and 2): inapplicable. Both attack search-tree size;
#    the tree averages 1.06-1.49 nodes on rejects and never exceeded 47 nodes
#    across 8.84 M real pairs. There is no subtree to avoid revisiting and no
#    product to turn into a sum.
#  * Hall-set and full Regin all-different filtering (survey technique 1,
#    beyond the forward checking already present): implemented in full and
#    verified against a brute-force oracle on 217,000 random configurations,
#    then measured. It found a genuine infeasibility the cheap filter had
#    missed in 221-245 cases out of ~3.8 M exact tests -- about 1 in 16,000 --
#    and moved neither subsume_nodes/subsume_calls nor
#    subsume_abstractions/subsume_calls outside run-to-run noise, while
#    costing 448-883 ns per call at n=10. NOT LANDED. The verified module is
#    preserved out-of-tree at .build/v3-tier2a/rejected/alldiff.rs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
